{"id":"debtor","name":"Debtor","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:debtor"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Debtor","text":"Various regulations as to the relation between debtor and creditor are laid down in the Scriptures. (1.) The debtor was to deliver up as a pledge to the creditor what he could most easily dispense with (Deut. 24:10, 11). (2.) A mill, or millstone, or upper garment, when given as a pledge, could not be kept over night (Ex. 22:26, 27). (3.) A debt could not be exacted during the Sabbatic year (Deut. 15:1-15). For other laws bearing on this relation see Lev. 25:14, 32, 39; Matt. 18:25, 34. (4.) A surety was liable in the same way as the original debtor (Prov. 11:15; 17:18)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4376","lemma":"מָכַר","xlit":"mâkar","gloss":"to sell, literally , or figuratively","kjv":"at all, sell","count":13,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H3104","lemma":"יוֹבֵל","xlit":"yôwbêl","gloss":"the blast of a horn","kjv":"jubile, ram's horn, trumpet","count":9,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H4465","lemma":"מִמְכָּר","xlit":"mimkâr","gloss":"merchandise","kjv":"ought, sale, that which...sold, ware","count":7,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H1353","lemma":"גְּאֻלָּה","xlit":"gᵉʼullâh","gloss":"redemption","kjv":"kindred, redeem, redemption, right","count":6,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H272","lemma":"אֲחֻזָּה","xlit":"ʼăchuzzâh","gloss":"something seized","kjv":"possession","count":7,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H1350","lemma":"גָּאַל","xlit":"gâʼal","gloss":"to be the next of kin","kjv":"in any wise, at all, avenger, deliver","count":7,"share":0.09}],"verses":["Lev.25.14","Lev.25.15","Lev.25.16","Lev.25.25","Lev.25.27","Lev.25.29","Lev.25.34","Lev.25.39","Lev.25.47","Lev.25.48","Lev.25.50","2Kgs.4.7","Neh.10.31","Exod.21.2","Exod.21.3","Exod.21.4","Exod.21.5","Exod.21.6","Exod.22.10","Exod.22.11","Exod.22.12","Exod.22.13","Exod.22.14","Exod.22.15","Lev.25.17","Lev.25.26","Lev.25.28","Lev.25.30","Lev.25.31","Lev.25.32","Lev.25.33","Lev.25.3